logical domain","start":2304,"end":2314,"description":"Lumenal"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":2315,"end":2335,"description":"Helical"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":2336,"end":2361,"description":"Cytoplasmic"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":2362,"end":2382,"description":"Helical"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":2383,"end":2405,"description":"Lumenal"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":2406,"end":2426,"description":"Helical"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":2427,"end":2448,"description":"Cytoplasmic"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":2449,"end":2469,"description":"Helical"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":2470,"end":2577,"description":"Lumenal"},{"type":"Region","start":2472,"end":2537,"description":"Interaction with ERP44"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":2512,"end":2512,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":2536,"end":2542,"description":""},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":2578,"end":2598,"description":"Helical"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":2599,"end":2758,"description":"Cytoplasmic"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2619,"end":2619,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2619,"end":2619,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2620,"end":2620,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2622,"end":2622,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2639,"end":2639,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2644,"end":2644,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2644,"end":2644,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2646,"end":2646,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2662,"end":2662,"description":"Ca(2+)"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Homotetramer (By similarity). Homodimer (By similarity). Interacts with ERP44 in a pH-, redox state- and calcium-dependent manner which results in the inhibition the calcium channel activity (PubMed:15652484). The strength of this interaction inversely correlates with calcium concentration (PubMed:15652484). Part of cGMP kinase signaling complex at least composed of ACTA2/alpha-actin, CNN1/calponin H1, PLN/phospholamban, PRKG1 and ITPR1 (By similarity). Interacts with IRAG1 (PubMed:16990611). Interacts with CABP1 (via N-terminus) (PubMed:12032348, PubMed:14685260). Interacts with TESPA1 (PubMed:23650607). Interacts (when not phosphorylated) with AHCYL1 (when phosphorylated); the interaction suppresses inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate binding to ITPR1 and is increased in the presence of BCL2L10 (PubMed:16793548, PubMed:27995898). Interacts with AHCYL2 (with lower affinity than with AHCYL1) (PubMed:19220705). Interacts with BCL2L10; the interaction is increased in the presence of AHCLY1 (PubMed:27995898). Interacts with BOK (via BH4 domain); protects ITPR1 from proteolysis by CASP3 during apoptosis (PubMed:23884412). Interacts with TRPC4 (By similarity). Interacts with CHGA and CHGB (By similarity). Interacts with CALM1; this interaction inhibits inositol 1,4,5 trisphosphate binding in both the presence and absence of calcium and 1,4,5 trisphosphate-induced calcium release in the presence of calcium (By similarity). Interacts with the complex composed by ERLIN1, ERLIN2 and RNF170 through ERLIN2; this interaction triggers its ubiquitin-proteasomal degradation (By similarity). Interacts with HSPA9; this interaction couples ITPR1 to VDAC1 (By similarity)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q14643-2","name":"2","synonyms":["SI-SIIISIIAC"],"notes":[],"length":2743,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000443694.5"],"refseq":["NM_001168272.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001161744.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,321],[322,337,2422]],"edits":[{"start":322,"end":336,"original":"FEEECLEFQPSVDPD","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":15,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":null,"foldedMissing":null,"features":[[0,15,0],[9,15,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":null},{"accession":"Q14643-3","name":"3","sy